# Keep the Intel LPSS I2C controller that carries the ELAN 04F3:311C touchpad
# (PCI 0000:00:15.1, bus i2c-6, nothing else on it) out of runtime suspend.
#
# 2026-09-06: the touchpad went silent mid-session — its interrupt line never
# fired — with every software layer healthy, and the controller sitting in
# runtime suspend. It came back after driver/controller resets with this set.
# Random I2C touchpad drop-outs on Intel laptops are the textbook symptom of the
# controller failing to leave suspend; keeping it awake costs negligible power.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", KERNEL=="0000:00:15.1", DRIVER=="intel-lpss", ATTR{power/control}="on"
